WEBVTT

00:01.334 --> 00:03.859
&lt;i>Previously on Two and a Half Men:&lt;/i>

00:04.037 --> 00:05.436
I'm asking you to marry me.

00:05.605 --> 00:07.937
We might as well just go to vegas
and elope.

00:08.108 --> 00:10.941
If we have a family, we'll need to turn
the second bedroom into a nursery.

00:11.111 --> 00:13.045
But that's... That's where Jake stays.

00:13.213 --> 00:16.046
But once Alan moves out,
Jake won't be staying there anymore.

00:16.216 --> 00:17.547
Alars moving out?

00:17.717 --> 00:20.618
Of course he is. Isn't he?

00:20.787 --> 00:22.618
I said, the wedding's off.

00:22.789 --> 00:25.121
- Can I borrow your wedding ring?
- What for?

00:25.425 --> 00:29.657
Oh, I thought as long as we're in vegas,
I'd marry Kandi. Ha.

00:30.029 --> 00:32.589
I pronounce you man and wife.
You may kiss the bride.

00:32.766 --> 00:34.700
I don't freaking believe it.

00:34.868 --> 00:37.928
Cheer up, Charlie. You're finally getting
what you always wanted.

00:38.104 --> 00:39.469
I'm moving out of your house.

00:39.639 --> 00:42.836
I don't freaking believe it.

00:45.478 --> 00:47.571
Do we have time to play roulette
before we go?

00:47.747 --> 00:51.012
Oh, honey, that is a sucker's game.
The odds are totally stacked against you.

00:51.184 --> 00:53.311
Ooh, Super Slots o'Fun Jackpot.

00:56.089 --> 00:58.922
Sure. Make the smart bet.

00:59.492 --> 01:01.483
Here, honey, kiss it before I put it in.

01:01.661 --> 01:04.425
And the honeymoon begins.

01:04.831 --> 01:08.733
Slots of fun, you get it? It's s-lots of fun.

01:09.769 --> 01:11.396
I'm ready for a refill.

01:17.443 --> 01:18.637
Is that good?

01:22.048 --> 01:24.243
I won. Ha-ha-ha!

01:24.884 --> 01:27.682
I won a half a million dollars.

01:30.023 --> 01:32.321
I don't freaking believe it.

01:33.092 --> 01:35.219
- Alan, you're rich.
- No, we're rich.

01:35.395 --> 01:37.488
We're married now,
what's mine is yours.

01:38.531 --> 01:40.260
Really?

01:40.433 --> 01:42.424
And the honeymoon ends.

02:07.460 --> 02:10.827
Uh, excuse me.
Do you know where Charlie is?

02:10.997 --> 02:12.794
Who's Charlie?

02:19.105 --> 02:20.504
Charlie, you in here?

02:21.574 --> 02:23.303
Hey, Alan.

02:23.476 --> 02:24.875
Long time no see.

02:25.044 --> 02:27.444
- Say hello to my brother, Alan.
- Hi, Alan.

02:27.614 --> 02:29.707
- Hi, Alan.
- Hi, Alan.

02:30.984 --> 02:32.178
Um...

02:32.352 --> 02:36.186
- I'm interrupting.
- Gee, you think?

02:37.657 --> 02:40.057
All right, listen,
I... I really need to talk to you.

02:40.226 --> 02:41.523
Can you come downstairs?

02:42.095 --> 02:43.687
Sure, give me...

02:45.164 --> 02:47.530
...an hour and a half.
- An hour and a half?

02:47.800 --> 02:50.894
I know it's a little rushed
but we're on a tight schedule here.

02:51.070 --> 02:54.130
Tina's got homework,
Cindy's gotta meet her fiancé and Marie...

02:54.307 --> 02:56.298
Well, Marie's on the clock.

02:56.476 --> 02:59.468
You had two women in bed
and felt the need to call a professional?

03:00.146 --> 03:02.137
Better safe than sorry.

03:02.749 --> 03:05.013
I see.
Well, I guess I'll just wait downstairs.

03:05.184 --> 03:09.211
Good call.
Because, you know, five's a crowd.

03:11.524 --> 03:14.789
Okay, does everybody remember
their assignment?

03:14.961 --> 03:16.792
- Yeah.
- Think so.

03:16.963 --> 03:19.090
Then let's do this thing.

03:31.311 --> 03:33.211
Hour and a half, on the dot.

03:34.380 --> 03:35.847
Can I plan or what?

03:37.550 --> 03:40.713
Hey, come on, show a little class.

03:44.123 --> 03:46.250
So how's the newlywed?

03:46.426 --> 03:48.587
- Still living the dream?
- Well...

03:48.761 --> 03:52.356
I gotta tell you, things haven't been
the same around here since you left.

03:52.532 --> 03:55.592
- That's nice but...
- Yeah, they've been way better.

03:55.935 --> 03:58.403
I mean, look around.
I don't even know these people.

04:01.307 --> 04:03.935
And I can have sex
in every room in the house now.

04:04.110 --> 04:07.910
I had forgotten how much fun you can have
on top of a washing machine. You know:

04:10.416 --> 04:12.475
- That does sound fun...
- And the best part is:

04:12.652 --> 04:15.246
Without Jake here,
Mom has no reason to visit.

04:15.421 --> 04:18.219
Heck, I may not have to see her again
until we meet in hell.

04:18.858 --> 04:21.554
- I'm happy for you.
- Come to think of it, without Jake...

04:21.728 --> 04:23.491
...there's no reason for you to visit.

04:23.930 --> 04:25.625
- I'm your brother.
- Yeah, so?

04:25.798 --> 04:27.493
I'm your brother, I don't visit you.

04:27.667 --> 04:29.259
Charlie, listen to me.

04:29.435 --> 04:30.663
My wife threw me out.

04:31.437 --> 04:33.905
Oh, dude. That's awful.

04:34.073 --> 04:35.472
Yeah.

04:37.076 --> 04:39.408
Well, thanks for stopping by.

04:40.213 --> 04:42.613
Arert you listening?
Kandi doesn't love me anymore.

04:42.782 --> 04:43.942
My marriage is over.

04:44.117 --> 04:45.482
My life is in ruins.

04:46.652 --> 04:47.676
Whoa.

04:48.287 --> 04:50.949
- What?
- Déjà vu.

04:52.658 --> 04:56.185
It's as if I've lived through this before
and didn't really enjoy it.

04:56.562 --> 04:59.531
- Charlie, I... I...
- But wait, there's a difference.

04:59.899 --> 05:02.459
You can get your own place
instead of sponging off me...

05:02.635 --> 05:04.728
...because you have money now, right?

05:04.904 --> 05:07.634
- Uh, well...
- oh, you suck.

05:07.807 --> 05:11.072
It wasrt my fault.
There were taxes and the condo...

05:11.244 --> 05:14.179
...and... And Kandi's new car
and Kandi's new clothes.

05:14.347 --> 05:17.316
And... And the shoes...
oh, God, so many shoes.

05:17.683 --> 05:19.014
How much do you have left?

05:24.323 --> 05:25.449
Eleven dollars.

05:25.892 --> 05:27.883
Okay, okay,
let's start from the beginning.

05:28.061 --> 05:31.155
- Things were fine until about a month ago...
- No, no, no.

05:31.330 --> 05:34.731
I'll go back upstairs, you knock on my door
and say you wanna talk to me.

05:34.901 --> 05:36.732
Only this time, I'll kill you.

05:37.870 --> 05:40.771
Oh, come on.
You're all I have left in this world.

05:40.940 --> 05:42.202
I need you, Charlie.

05:46.913 --> 05:49.143
Anybody here know a Charlie?

05:55.354 --> 05:57.845
Oh, jeez.

05:58.024 --> 06:00.822
I'm working for Caligula.

06:05.998 --> 06:08.091
- Hi, Berta.
- Hey, Zippy.

06:08.267 --> 06:10.531
What are you doing here?

06:11.070 --> 06:13.732
My marriage is over.
Kandi kicked me out.

06:14.273 --> 06:15.934
Damn, that's horrible.

06:16.109 --> 06:17.371
Yeah.

06:17.743 --> 06:20.405
Damn, damn, damn.

06:20.580 --> 06:23.743
- Tell me about it.
- I had october in the pool.

06:27.286 --> 06:30.483
- Pool? What...? What pool?
- Me, your brother, your mom...

06:30.656 --> 06:34.956
...a couple of neighbors had a pool
on how long before she dumped your ass.

06:35.228 --> 06:36.718
I was so close.

06:36.896 --> 06:38.864
You were betting
my marriage would fail?

06:39.031 --> 06:42.023
No, we were betting on when.

06:43.536 --> 06:45.299
So Charlie took you back, huh?

06:45.471 --> 06:48.599
Well, not with open arms
or an open heart...

06:48.774 --> 06:50.332
...or even an open door.

06:50.510 --> 06:53.377
After he pushed me out,
I had to climb in through the window.

06:55.148 --> 06:56.445
But, yeah, I'm back.

06:56.782 --> 06:58.113
Well, I'm glad.

06:59.051 --> 07:01.952
- You're kidding.
- No. With you and the kid around...

07:02.121 --> 07:04.885
...I won't have to hose down
the washing machine so often.

07:06.626 --> 07:07.957
I'll get that.

07:13.466 --> 07:16.731
I guess there's no trusting
this butter now.

07:18.371 --> 07:20.737
Or the loose bananas.

07:25.411 --> 07:27.811
- Hello, Alan.
- Judith.

07:28.247 --> 07:29.271
Hey, Dad.

07:29.582 --> 07:30.913
Hey, buddy.

07:35.588 --> 07:38.580
So is somebody gonna explain to me
what the heck is going on?

07:40.459 --> 07:42.859
I thought he should hear it from you.

07:43.029 --> 07:44.428
Okay.

07:44.597 --> 07:48.533
Jake, listen,
I know you liked Kandi very much...

07:48.701 --> 07:52.262
...but she and I have decided
that we really can't stay married.

07:52.605 --> 07:53.663
Oh, man.

07:53.839 --> 07:58.173
- It doesn't mean that you can't be friends.
- No, I had December.

08:01.781 --> 08:06.343
Alan, I just wanna say I'm very sorry
things didn't work out for you and Kandi.

08:06.919 --> 08:08.284
Thanks.

08:09.822 --> 08:11.221
You won the pool, didn't you?

08:12.058 --> 08:13.582
Yeah.

08:13.759 --> 08:15.590
And just FYI, I spoke to my lawyer.

08:15.761 --> 08:18.229
Even if Kandi takes you
for everything you've got...

08:18.397 --> 08:20.831
...you still have to pay me alimony.
Here's his bill.

08:24.804 --> 08:27.136
Ha! Six hundred dollars?

08:27.306 --> 08:29.706
He explained it very slowly.

08:39.418 --> 08:41.579
- You didn't call.
- What?

08:41.754 --> 08:45.121
When Dad moved out, you said you and me
could get together and do stuff.

08:45.291 --> 08:46.883
But you never called.

08:47.560 --> 08:49.687
Ah, jeez, Jake, I'm sorry.

08:49.962 --> 08:51.554
I waited.

08:52.198 --> 08:53.256
I'll make it up to you.

08:53.633 --> 08:55.225
- When?
- Later.

08:59.605 --> 09:01.539
I'm still here.

09:02.775 --> 09:05.209
- What do you want me to do, Jake?
- I don't know.

09:05.378 --> 09:07.573
You really let me down
and it hurt my feelings.

09:07.847 --> 09:09.678
I know. I feel awful.

09:09.849 --> 09:11.783
Fifty bucks and it goes away.

09:13.219 --> 09:14.243
- Ten.
- Done.

09:15.888 --> 09:17.412
Love you, Uncle Charlie.

09:17.957 --> 09:19.822
Back at you.

09:26.132 --> 09:28.123
How long is he gonna sit out there?

09:28.301 --> 09:30.496
I don't know, Jake.
He's pretty depressed.

09:30.836 --> 09:34.670
Yeah. Well, that's the price you pay
when you think with your penis.

09:35.841 --> 09:38.935
- Did you hear that from your mother?
- No, your mother.

09:40.313 --> 09:42.645
- And how are you feeling about all this?
- I'm okay.

09:42.815 --> 09:46.683
- Are you sure?
- Uncle Charlie, this is not my first divorce.

09:47.553 --> 09:48.645
Got it.

09:48.821 --> 09:51.585
I'll tell you one thing, though,
I am never getting married.

09:51.757 --> 09:53.520
That's a sweet dream to have, Jake.

09:54.627 --> 09:57.425
Sooner or later, you'll meet a girl
who's smart, beautiful...

09:57.596 --> 09:59.996
...and has a real grudge
against her parents.

10:00.166 --> 10:02.964
- What are you gonna do then?
- Don't worry, I have a plan.

10:03.135 --> 10:05.763
- Really?
- Yeah, if a girl falls in love with me...

10:05.938 --> 10:10.170
...I'll tell her I can't marry till I have enough
money, even though I'll be secretly rich.

10:10.876 --> 10:12.776
How do you plan to get secretly rich?

10:12.945 --> 10:15.470
I'm gonna marry a movie star.

10:17.016 --> 10:20.042
You're gonna marry a movie star
to avoid getting married?

10:21.420 --> 10:23.684
I guess I haven't worked out
all the bugs.

10:24.323 --> 10:27.156
Well, keep me posted.

10:32.064 --> 10:33.395
Hey.

10:33.566 --> 10:34.999
Hey.

10:36.702 --> 10:38.932
Jake sure changed
in the last few months.

10:39.105 --> 10:42.199
- I'm starting to see a real little man there.
- Mm-hm.

10:43.509 --> 10:45.875
Not a real bright little man.

10:47.113 --> 10:49.206
- So, what you doing?
- Making plans.

10:49.715 --> 10:52.582
- Do they involve marrying a movie star?
- What?

10:52.752 --> 10:54.913
Nothing. Nothing. What's your plan?

10:55.087 --> 10:59.547
Well, I figured I'd have a nice big lunch,
get real drunk...

10:59.725 --> 11:03.388
...stroll down to the beach
and try to swim to Japan.

11:03.696 --> 11:05.027
Oh.

11:05.197 --> 11:06.221
Why the lunch?

11:06.599 --> 11:10.035
I wanna cramp up and drown
before the sharks rip me to shreds.

11:10.469 --> 11:13.063
Well, keep me posted.

11:14.039 --> 11:16.405
I'm a failure, Charlie.

11:16.909 --> 11:22.472
Everything I've tried to do in my life
has ended in complete, abject failure.

11:22.648 --> 11:24.673
Buddy, you're looking at this
the wrong way.

11:24.850 --> 11:28.411
See, I've failed again.

11:28.788 --> 11:30.847
Will you shut up and listen to me?

11:31.023 --> 11:33.014
Failure is nothing to be ashamed of.

11:33.192 --> 11:35.592
It's a part of life. It's how we learn.

11:35.761 --> 11:37.388
Well, you know what?

11:37.563 --> 11:39.929
I've failed for almost 40 years...

11:40.099 --> 11:41.760
...and what have I learned?

11:44.870 --> 11:47.395
Oh, that wasrt a rhetorical question?

11:48.641 --> 11:52.042
Come on, Alan, you gotta have
a sense of humor about this.

11:52.211 --> 11:56.079
A broke-ass, middle-aged guy
marries a 22-year-old knucklehead...

11:56.248 --> 11:58.773
...just before he wins
a half a million dollars?

11:58.951 --> 12:02.216
And then she takes him
for everything he's got? Heh.

12:02.388 --> 12:04.117
That's hilarious.

12:05.658 --> 12:08.684
Okay, okay.
Okay, maybe you're too close to it now...

12:08.861 --> 12:10.294
...but trust me, it's funny.

12:14.066 --> 12:15.761
Mm...

12:19.371 --> 12:20.736
Where are you going?

12:20.906 --> 12:23.067
The ocears that way.

12:31.984 --> 12:34.452
The kid and I are going to the movies,
you wanna come?

12:34.620 --> 12:35.780
No, thanks.

12:35.955 --> 12:38.116
- Can I get you something to eat?
- No.

12:38.290 --> 12:40.258
- Something to drink?
- No.

12:40.426 --> 12:42.485
How about
a bottle of Scotch and a hooker?

12:43.729 --> 12:45.287
I just wanna be alone.

12:45.464 --> 12:47.557
Well, you don't need my help for that.

12:47.733 --> 12:49.325
That's your home run swing.

12:49.502 --> 12:51.697
Just close the door on the way out.

12:51.871 --> 12:55.204
Fine, I'll close it.
Then I'll nail it shut and plaster it over...

12:55.374 --> 12:59.333
...and hang a picture of something
a little more cheerful. Like a plane crash.

13:02.748 --> 13:04.340
Okay.

13:04.550 --> 13:07.144
I am through feeling sorry for myself.

13:10.656 --> 13:12.248
Maybe not.

13:16.662 --> 13:17.686
Alan?

13:17.863 --> 13:20.229
Oh, terrific.

13:20.533 --> 13:23.969
Charlie told me about you and Kandi.
I'm so sorry.

13:24.136 --> 13:25.865
Yeah, well, thanks.

13:26.038 --> 13:27.869
Did he also tell you I wanna be alone?

13:28.240 --> 13:29.935
Yes, he did.

13:30.109 --> 13:32.737
So want some company?

13:34.680 --> 13:36.648
- No.
- How about a hug?

13:36.815 --> 13:39.283
Is it a goodbye hug?

13:41.186 --> 13:44.883
Alan, I know what it's like
to lose at love.

13:45.624 --> 13:47.819
- Rose?
- Yes, baby?

13:48.494 --> 13:50.519
You're a stalker.

13:51.664 --> 13:54.189
We prefer to be called
boundary challenged.

13:56.735 --> 13:57.759
Just go away.

13:58.070 --> 13:59.537
Go away? Ha.

13:59.705 --> 14:01.536
Alan, I'm a stalker.

14:03.742 --> 14:06.506
Trust me, this pain will pass.

14:06.679 --> 14:09.204
The aching emptiness
that's swallowing up your heart...

14:09.381 --> 14:11.508
...will be transformed
into something beautiful.

14:11.984 --> 14:13.576
What's that?

14:16.188 --> 14:18.179
Resentment.

14:20.092 --> 14:22.788
A burning, white-hot resentment...

14:22.962 --> 14:27.160
...that empowers you to commit
unspeakable acts of revenge.

14:28.767 --> 14:31.065
You're gonna want a scrapbook.

14:38.143 --> 14:40.236
- Dad?
- Yeah?

14:40.412 --> 14:43.040
Uncle Charlie's gonna take me back
to Mom's now.

14:43.215 --> 14:45.615
Well, come in here and say goodbye.

14:47.052 --> 14:48.542
Bye.

14:48.954 --> 14:51.752
That's it?
Come here and give your old dad a hug.

14:58.897 --> 15:00.228
That's better.

15:01.600 --> 15:02.794
You still depressed?

15:02.968 --> 15:05.027
Oh, no, no. I'm fine.

15:05.537 --> 15:06.731
Just taking a little nap.

15:06.905 --> 15:09.169
You've been napping for two days.

15:09.341 --> 15:11.206
I'm getting old, Jake.

15:11.377 --> 15:13.777
Old people nap a lot.

15:14.213 --> 15:16.773
It's kind of a dry run for death.

15:17.116 --> 15:18.174
Okay.

15:18.350 --> 15:19.908
Well, see you.

15:20.085 --> 15:21.643
See you.

15:21.954 --> 15:24.081
- Hey, Dad?
- Yeah?

15:24.423 --> 15:27.586
Even though Mom stopped loving you
and Kandi stopped loving you...

15:27.760 --> 15:29.455
...you don't have to worry about me.

15:29.628 --> 15:30.652
Thanks, pal.

15:30.829 --> 15:32.854
You're my dad.
I pretty much gotta love you.

15:38.070 --> 15:42.166
So is he still curled up
like a cocktail shrimp?

15:42.708 --> 15:43.800
Yep.

15:44.143 --> 15:46.668
This was a real fun weekend.

15:47.179 --> 15:49.773
Wait in the car, Jake,
and I'll be right there.

15:50.716 --> 15:53.412
Okay, I am running out of patience
with this guy.

15:53.585 --> 15:56.247
I've had relationships end
and I don't go crawling into bed over it.

15:57.623 --> 16:00.217
Yeah, yeah, yeah,
you know what I mean.

16:00.626 --> 16:03.686
- It may not be just the relationship.
- What are you talking about?

16:04.029 --> 16:07.863
Charlie, I've studied psychology
for eight years and been a patient for 20.

16:09.968 --> 16:13.460
Your brother is exhibiting
all the classic signs of clinical depression.

16:13.872 --> 16:15.931
What, you think
he might try to hurt himself?

16:16.108 --> 16:18.167
The important question is,
do we stop him?

16:20.646 --> 16:23.206
Oh, like I'm the only one here
thinking that.

16:26.618 --> 16:28.586
All right,
I didn't wanna have to do this.

16:28.754 --> 16:30.654
Desperate times call
for desperate measures.

16:30.823 --> 16:33.519
- What are you gonna do?
- Something I hoped I'd never have to.

16:33.692 --> 16:36.991
- You don't mean...
- I'm afraid so.

16:37.596 --> 16:38.654
Hello?

16:38.831 --> 16:40.389
Mom?

16:43.569 --> 16:47.505
Oh, God, what plague
have you set upon me now?

16:47.806 --> 16:50.434
EvELYN:
Alan, it's Mommy.

16:52.878 --> 16:54.573
Good one.

16:56.548 --> 16:59.847
Oh, my poor darling.

17:00.819 --> 17:02.650
How are you holding up?

17:02.821 --> 17:04.254
How do you think?

17:04.423 --> 17:06.254
I blew another marriage.

17:06.425 --> 17:09.792
I wasted all my money.
I'm a complete and utter failure.

17:09.962 --> 17:13.693
Oh, sweetie, you just can't see
the big picture, can you?

17:13.866 --> 17:15.094
What big picture?

17:15.267 --> 17:19.795
Every foolish choice you've made,
every wasted opportunity...

17:20.139 --> 17:23.905
...every hapless misstep in your sad,
misbegotten life...

17:24.076 --> 17:25.236
I know, I know.

17:25.978 --> 17:28.276
It's an opportunity to learn and grow.

17:28.881 --> 17:33.409
Well, perhaps. But more importantly,
it's a reflection on me.

17:34.286 --> 17:36.447
Always good to see you, Mom.

17:36.789 --> 17:39.781
- I'm not finished.
- Of course not.

17:40.259 --> 17:42.727
There is a silver lining
in this dark cloud.

17:42.895 --> 17:45.728
I can't wait to hear about it.

17:47.232 --> 17:52.636
You're all alone, you're penniless
and you have no prospects.

17:52.971 --> 17:56.065
Are we at the silver-lining part yet?

17:56.241 --> 17:57.299
Yes.

17:57.476 --> 18:03.005
Short of contracting a flesh-eating disease,
things couldn't possibly get any worse.

18:04.416 --> 18:06.179
You've hit rock bottom.

18:06.351 --> 18:08.751
You have nowhere to go but up.

18:10.455 --> 18:11.945
You know what?

18:12.391 --> 18:13.915
You're right.

18:14.827 --> 18:18.024
You're self-obsessed, insensitive
and soul-sucking, but you're right.

18:20.966 --> 18:23.696
I have stared into the abyss...

18:23.869 --> 18:25.666
...and I'm still here.

18:25.838 --> 18:29.865
L... I've had my heart shattered
and then shattered again...

18:30.042 --> 18:32.442
...and I'm still here.

18:32.644 --> 18:36.102
I've taken every piece of crap
that life could throw at me...

18:36.281 --> 18:37.373
...and I'm still here.

18:37.549 --> 18:40.848
&lt;i>Well, we don't have to turn this into
An Evening with Liza Minnelli.&lt;/i>

18:43.755 --> 18:46.485
Now, get washed, get dressed...

18:46.658 --> 18:49.126
...get on with your life.
- Okay.

18:49.294 --> 18:54.061
And remember, no matter what,
I'll always love you.

18:54.433 --> 18:57.368
- I know. Thanks.
- Oh, don't thank me, sweetheart.

18:57.703 --> 19:01.036
I'm your mother, I have to love you.

19:11.183 --> 19:12.275
Hey.

19:13.418 --> 19:16.285
- Hey.
- Thanks for taking Jake back to Judith's.

19:16.455 --> 19:17.820
No problem.

19:17.990 --> 19:19.582
Sorry I had to send Mom in there.

19:19.758 --> 19:21.282
No, no, you did the right thing.

19:21.460 --> 19:23.485
I needed a good slap in the face.

19:23.662 --> 19:27.154
Although with Mom,
it's more like a nail gun to the testicles.

19:30.135 --> 19:31.568
That was my thinking.

19:31.737 --> 19:34.570
Well, I'm really grateful.

19:34.740 --> 19:36.503
Don't mention it.

19:37.943 --> 19:39.308
So...

19:39.478 --> 19:40.877
...look at us, huh?

19:41.046 --> 19:43.480
Just like old times. Ha.

19:43.649 --> 19:45.014
Yep.

19:46.084 --> 19:48.917
The Harper brothers, together again.

19:49.321 --> 19:50.948
Uh-huh.

19:51.123 --> 19:55.253
The chicks will come and go but you and I
will always be there for each other.

19:55.827 --> 19:57.226
Sure.

19:58.563 --> 19:59.962
Forever.

20:03.368 --> 20:07.327
Not literally till the end of time
but, you know, till one of us dies.

20:09.508 --> 20:12.944
It will probably be you because you don't
take very good care of yourself.

20:14.579 --> 20:16.069
Gotcha.

20:18.517 --> 20:20.075
Fist me.

20:24.723 --> 20:26.350
You want me to fist you?

20:26.792 --> 20:29.727
You know, like the bros in the 'hood.

20:31.229 --> 20:34.528
We're the bros and this is our 'hood.

20:39.371 --> 20:41.430
Pow! Right on.

20:44.876 --> 20:47.344
Tell you what, I will grab us
a couple of brewskies...

20:47.512 --> 20:50.640
...so that Team Harper
can kick back and chill.

20:50.816 --> 20:52.477
- Terrific.
- Uh...

20:52.651 --> 20:55.313
Well, actually, I am more in the mood
for a chardonnay...

20:55.487 --> 20:57.182
...but I'll get you a beer.

20:57.389 --> 20:58.447
Okay.

20:58.623 --> 21:02.354
Oh, uh, maybe I'll make a nice little plate
of cheese and crackers.

21:02.527 --> 21:04.222
Nothing fancy.

21:04.629 --> 21:06.426
- Good.
- Ooh.

21:06.598 --> 21:08.190
Uh, I don't suppose you have any Brie.

21:10.635 --> 21:12.398
I don't know.

21:13.238 --> 21:16.901
Not important.
You relax, I got you covered. Pow!
